 [17592186569881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569881 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569881 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569881 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186569783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569881 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5be30950-b64e-577a-ae02-66dc69074ea6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186569720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569945 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eda18abf-1e9e-51ea-a1af-55bc7948bea6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569961 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569961 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569961 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569961 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=4 \\\\ y-3z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569961 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d9a8a04-d6f4-5dae-8ede-86bd3b61ce86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569961 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5z &=2 \\\\ y-3z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5z+2 \\\\ y &=3z-1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5z+2 \\\\ 3z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569976 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569976 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569976 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569976 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+y &=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y &=3 \\\\ -x-4y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is inconsistent\n\nII. The system has a unique solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569976 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569978 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 4x-8y &=4 \\\\ -4x+8y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569978 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2y+1 \\\\ y &=y,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y+1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
